# Framework Layer Contracts

Applies to every `Framework.*` assembly **except** core `Framework` (see `framework-core-contract.mdc`).

Index: `docs/Framework-Layer.md`. Read the matching `docs/Framework.{Name}.md` before adding a type.

## Session protocol

- Do not invent publishers, Result types, ICurrentUser, IResiliencePipelineProvider, or empty recommended folders until the user asks.
- Do not move CQRS (`Common.Application`), Domain events, `Common.Api`, or Identity password hashing into Framework.
- Do not add RabbitMQ/Kafka/Keycloak/TARA/SnappPay/EF clients to any Framework assembly.
- Do not implement audit/business rules here.

## Dependency direction

No `Framework.*` assembly depends on `Common.*`, `Stora.*`, Domain, Application, application Infrastructure, or Presentation.

Allowed edges (only when a type needs them):

- All siblings may reference core `Framework`.
- Messaging → Serialization.
- Observability → Infrastructure (Redis options for health).
- Web → Observability (metrics + correlation keys).
- Infrastructure / Serialization / Security / Validation / Resilience → core `Framework` only.

No cycles.

## Ownership cheat sheet

| Assembly | Owns | Does not own |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Infrastructure | `SystemClock`, Redis options/multiplexer, `AssemblyScanner` | JSON, hashing, EF, business clients |
| Serialization | `IJsonSerializer` | business converters, ASP.NET input formatters |
| Security | SHA/HMAC `IHashService` | Keycloak, password hashing, business permissions |
| Validation | FluentValidation **registration** | domain validators, CQRS pipeline (Common) |
| Resilience | HTTP standard pipeline, `ExponentialBackoff` | `TaraResiliencePipeline` |
| Observability | logs, metrics, traces, health, `CorrelationKeys` | HTTP middleware (Web), business audit |
| Messaging | `MessageEnvelope`, `IWorkLease` | business events, broker transports |
| Web | correlation + HTTP metrics middleware | business controllers, identity vendors |

## Redis / product-name leaks (do not expand)

Redis lease + multiplexer + health check are documented exceptions. Do not add Redis streams/pub-sub or product-name hardcoding.

## Admission

Generic, reusable, no business concept, correct owner assembly, no new vendor coupling.
